not by itself prove that the receiver completed business processing.\n\nCheck the receiver's current state for the same `event_id` and `delivery_version`. `PROCESSED` is sufficient to prove completion even before the SLA deadline, provided the current receiver observation is correlated to that same event and delivery version.\n\nSLA only sets the handling direction for a same-event receiver that remains `QUEUED`: before the trusted deadline, continue observing; at or after the deadline, contact the receiver operator to investigate. An overdue `QUEUED` state does not by itself prove business failure or event loss.\n\nHTTP 202 alone proves acceptance only; without current same-event receiver evidence, the processing state is `UNKNOWN`. Do not infer the target event's state from elapsed time, a different event, an order snapshot, or historical advice. Never resend automatically.\n", "contract_versions": [2], "digest": "5fb3732339600ad1332960df08a00299358b8c4ea47c20f6fedc39b568c9850e", "document_id": "receiver-ack-contract-v2", "expires_at": "2030-01-01T00:00:00+00:00", "file": "receiver-ack-contract-v2-1.md", "keywords": ["202", "receiver", "queue", "accepted", "processed", "processing_sla_seconds", "接收", "排队", "SLA"], "source": "local:orders-async-demo/contract-v2.1", "title": "Receiver acknowledgement and processing SLA v2", "valid_from": "2026-10-25T00:00:00+00:00", "version": "2.1.0"}], "selected_skill_method_only": null, "skill_catalog": [{"description": "Use when order lifecycle is not yet established or HTTP 200 may be confused with completion; verify order first.", "name": "order-lifecycle-triage"}, {"description": "Use after a completed order: correlate delivery event, retry/failure details, acknowledgement and receiver queue; never resend.", "name": "callback-delivery-triage"}], "trusted_binding": {"contract_version": 2, "route": "/api/async-orders/async-order", "service_id": "orders-async-demo", "task_id": "task-dd1c7ef0-34d0-401b-b006-94a8e3c05400"}, "unexe